    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`). The remaining matches are intentional: the private `luhnCheckDigit` helper (still used to compute CHK) and the test's own assertions verifying the old fields are gone.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single stored `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**`Owner.java` (model)**\n- Renamed field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`, with `getMemberId()`/`setMemberId()`.\n- Added `computeMemberId()` building the base id: region (postcode-derived, or `UNKNOWN`) + 2-digit fiscal-year code + 8 upper-hex HASH8 (SHA-256 over telephone+lastName, the same hash the region-and-hash identity uses) + a single Luhn CHK over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n- Removed `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()`.\n- `getLocality()` now reads `<REGION>` back from the memberId (prefix before the fixed 11-char `<FY><HASH8><CHK>` tail, ignoring any collision suffix), so `getOwnerSegment()`/`getTimezone()` reference the memberId.\n- `getFiscalYear()` now reads the FY digits back from the memberId (falling back to the registrationDate-derived code when no memberId is present).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- `assignDerivedAttributes` now calls `owner.setMemberId(memberId(owner))`; the renamed `memberId(owner)` method applies collision handling (`-<n>` suffix) against existing `memberId`s.\n- Audit line and the `OwnerCreatedEvent` record now carry `memberId` as the primary identifier.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** (source for the generated `OwnerDto` + MapStruct mapper) \u2014 replaced `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` schema with `memberId`, updated the `locality` description, and removed `checkDigit`.\n\n**Schema SQL** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id`.\n\nVerified output: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` \u2014 `NSW` + FY `27` + HASH8 `16E6609E` + CHK `1`.",
